I was just wondering if it should be an *exception*.  It would seem that
asking for a wish isn't like writing out an invoice.  I mean we're talking
about barbarians here, literacy may not be their strong point.  I can
imagine letting out a Genie who says ("You freed me.")

Genie:   Oh, you set me free, let me give you a wish.  What would you like?
Krusty:  gray dragon scale mail, please
Genie:   Excuse me, how do you spell that?


On the other thread, (wishing only for things you have found):

I don't see why anyone would want to wish at all if they could only wish
for things they had found.  Well, not *at all*, but the only things that
would be useful to wish for would be scrolls and potions.  Other 'good
magic' would be dependent on whether you found it yet or not.  Certainly
you wouldn't really need it to get the same kind of armor or weapon that
you already found (unless a black dragon has been breathing).

